---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import {
  siteConfig,
  homeUrl,
  siteHost,
  renderTemplate,
  legalUpdatedLabel,
} from '../lib/site';

const { appName, contactDisplay: contact } = siteConfig;

const sections = [
  { id: 'scope', label: 'What this covers' },
  { id: 'notice', label: 'Sending a notice' },
  { id: 'where', label: 'Where to send it' },
  { id: 'counter', label: 'Counter-notice' },
  { id: 'repeat', label: 'Repeat notices' },
  { id: 'notes', label: 'Notes' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title={siteConfig.pages.dmca.title}
  description={renderTemplate(siteConfig.pages.dmca.description)}
  heading="DMCA and takedown"
  lede="How to report material you believe infringes your rights, what a notice must contain, and how it is handled."
  updated={legalUpdatedLabel}
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="scope">What this covers</h2>
  <p>
    This page explains how {siteHost} handles copyright complaints about the website and about the
    {appName} release it publishes. The website itself does not host, store or transmit video. The
    APK is served by an external download host, and that host accepts notices about the file
    directly as well.
  </p>
  <p>
    A notice about a specific stream or broadcast should identify the material clearly. Availability
    of a stream inside the app varies by region, and this page cannot confirm what a particular
    source will show.
  </p>

  <h2 id="notice">Sending a notice</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe material on this site or in the published release infringes your copyright, send
    a written notice that includes all of the following:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      a physical or electronic signature of the copyright owner or a person authorised to act for
      them;
    </li>
    <li>identification of the copyrighted work you say has been infringed, or a representative list of works;</li>
    <li>
      enough information to locate the material: the exact URL on this site, or the app version and
      package name if the complaint is about the release;
    </li>
    <li>your name, address, telephone number and email address;</li>
    <li>
      a statement that you have a good-faith belief that the use is not authorised by the copyright
      owner, its agent or the law;
    </li>
    <li>
      a statement, under penalty of perjury, that the information in the notice is accurate and that
      you are the copyright owner or are authorised to act for them.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Notices that omit these elements may be returned so they can be completed. Deliberately false or
    abusive notices may be rejected.
  </p>

  <h2 id="where">Where to send it</h2>
  <p>
    Send notices to the address published on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>:{' '}
    <a href={homeUrl}>{contact}</a>. Put “DMCA notice” in the subject line and include the URL or
    version you are writing about.
  </p>
  <p>
    The external host that serves the APK also runs its own complaint process. Contacting that host
    as well is usually the fastest way to have a specific file reviewed, because it can act on the
    file directly.
  </p>

  <h2 id="counter">Counter-notice</h2>
  <p>
    If material was removed and you believe it was removed by mistake or misidentification, you can
    send a counter-notice. It should include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>your physical or electronic signature;</li>
    <li>identification of the material that was removed and where it appeared before removal;</li>
    <li>
      a statement, under penalty of perjury, that you have a good-faith belief the material was
      removed by mistake or misidentification;
    </li>
    <li>your name, address and telephone number, and consent to the jurisdiction of a competent court;</li>
    <li>a statement that you will accept service of process from the person who sent the original notice.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A counter-notice is reviewed on the same basis as a notice. Where the law allows, material may be
    restored if the original complainant does not take further action.
  </p>

  <h2 id="repeat">Repeat notices</h2>
  <p>
    Notices are recorded. If the same source or file is the subject of repeated valid notices, the
    related material can be removed and further publication of that build can be declined.
  </p>

  <h2 id="notes">Notes</h2>
  <p>
    This page describes the process in plain language. It is not legal advice, and it does not
    replace the requirements of the Digital Millennium Copyright Act or any other law that applies
    to you.
  </p>
  <p>
    For general copyright and trademark information, see the <a href="/copyright/">copyright page</a>.
    For anything else, use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
